Unreleased - se7enxweb/expcomponents-archive
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Updated: Requirements on other Zeta Components point to their Exponential
  forks (se7enxweb/expcomponents-base), which replace the upstream packages.
- Updated: composer.json states the license (Apache-2.0) and the PHP
  versions; the component is tested on PHP 7.4 to 8.5.
- Added: NOTICE keeps the upstream copyright notices and names the fork;
  README.md describes the fork.


1.5.2 - Tuesday 3 November 2026
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Renamed: The package is now se7enxweb/expcomponents-archive (repository
  github.com/se7enxweb/expcomponents-archive), a maintained fork of
  zetacomponents/Archive. It replaces zetacomponents/archive, so existing
  requirements keep working; the class names (ezcArchive*) are unchanged.
- Fixed: No deprecation notices on PHP 8.1 to 8.5. Parameters with a null
  default are explicitly nullable, the Iterator methods carry
  #[\ReturnTypeWillChange], and ezcArchiveEntry no longer passes null to
  substr(), strlen() or strcmp() for an entry without a link.
- Fixed: Reading a tar header no longer passes space or NUL padding to
  octdec() (deprecated since PHP 7.4); the decoded values are the same.
- Fixed: The CRC-32 table used for Zip archives is built as an array from
  the start, instead of turning false into an array (deprecated since
  PHP 8.1). An error handler that throws on deprecations left the table
  incomplete, with "Undefined array key" warnings after it.
- Fixed: Long file names and long link names in GNU tar archives no longer
  keep the terminating NUL byte, so such entries extract again (PHP 8 refused
  the name with a ValueError, PHP 7 could not find the link target).
- Fixed: Appending to a ustar archive no longer raises a notice when the
  file's user or group ID has no entry in the user or group database; the
  name is written empty, as before.
- Added: A test that loads every class in a fresh process and fails on any
  deprecation, and a GitHub Actions workflow running the suite on PHP 7.4
  to 8.5.


1.5.1 - Thursday 23 February 2023
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

- Removed an unused line which generates an error in PHP 7.2.
